{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
'Tis the [G]last rose of [C]summer,
[G]Left blooming a[D]lone;
All her [G]lovely com[C]panions
Are [G]faded [D]and [G]gone;
No [Em]flower of her [Bm]kindred,
No [C]rosebud is [D]nigh,
To re[G]flect back her [C]blushes,
Or [G]give sigh [D]for [G]sigh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
I'll [G]not leave thee, thou [C]lone one!
To [G]pine on the [D]stem;
Since the [G]lovely are [C]sleeping,
Go, [G]sleep thou [D]with [G]them.
Thus [Em]kindly I [Bm]scatter
Thy [C]leaves o'er the [D]bed,
Where thy [G]mates of the [C]garden
Lie [G]scentless [D]and [G]dead.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
So [G]soon may I [C]follow,
When [G]friendships de[D]cay,
And from [G]Love's shining [C]circle
The [G]gems drop [D]a[G]way.
When [Em]true hearts lie [Bm]withered,
And [C]fond ones are [D]flown,
Oh! [G]who would in[C]habit
This [G]bleak world [D]a[G]lone?
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: G}
